# Cyber-Physical Architecture & Triage Pipeline

### 1. Biomedical Signal Conditioning Pipeline
Raw physiological signals collected across the physical interface are filtered to strip shop-floor electromagnetic interference (EMI) and powerline artifacts:

1. **ECG Lead-II Conditioning:** Analog front-end instrumentation amplifier (AD8232 / ADS1292) providing a Common-Mode Rejection Ratio ($\text{CMRR} > 100\text{ dB}$). Bandpass filtered ($0.5\text{--}40\text{ Hz}$) to eliminate baseline wander and electromyographic (EMG) muscle tremors.
2. **Photoplethysmogram (PPG):** High-efficiency red ($\lambda = 660\text{ nm}$) and infrared ($\lambda = 940\text{ nm}$) reflectance photodiode matrix (MAX30102). Ambient light cancellation removes 50 Hz/60 Hz ambient flicker.
3. **Non-Contact Pyrometry:** Melexis MLX90614 factory-calibrated infrared thermopile sensor with internal 17-bit ADC, reading body temperature within $\pm 0.2^\circ\text{C}$ accuracy.

